# Protected and generated assets must remain outside source control.
#
# Defence in depth: the private workspace is a sibling of this
# repository, these patterns keep generated and sensitive files out of Git
# candidates, and the publication audit re-checks candidates, the staged
# index and history. A leading "/" anchors a pattern to the repository
# root; other patterns apply at any depth. Names that are unambiguously
# generated or private are ignored at any depth; data, models and similar
# names only at the root, so source and test packages such as tests/data
# stay trackable (their weight and data files are still excluded by
# extension). Source, docs, configuration, tests and synthetic fixtures
# (for example tests/fixtures/synthetic_*.json) stay trackable.

# -- Protected, source, patient, case, evaluation, audit and output data ----
protected-data/
/protected-data/
protected_data/
patient-data/
patient_data/
patient-graphs/
patient_graphs/
source-exports/
source_exports/
cases/
evaluation/
evaluations/
audit/
audits/
outputs/
/outputs/
output/
results/
runs/
logs/
/data/
/graphs/
/exports/
/extracts/
/patients/
/private/
/secrets/

